            <ArticleTitle>Analysis of circumferential lumbar fusion outcome in the treatment of degenerative disc disease of the lumbar spine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>472-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study reviews the results of circumferential fusion in patients with degenerative disc disease who are at high risk for achieving spinal fusion. The fusion rate was 100% and the satisfactory clinical outcome slightly more than 50% in a patient population known to have high risk factors for a poor outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
